    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFollow-up to #64984. GLM-4.1V/4.5V (and GLM-OCR and GLM-5.3-Flash, which inherit its config) and Kimi-K2.5 have the same FlashInfer `cu_seqlens` misalignment in encoder CUDA graph replay. This registers the existing `_pad_flashinfer_cu_seqlens_buffer` for both.\n\n## Claims\n\n- GLM-4.1V family: with video enabled, capture pads `cu_seqlens` to `max_frames_per_batch`, but image replays pad to `max_batch_size`. With FlashInfer backend, image replays then result in a smaller batch bucket than the capture.\n- Kimi-K2.5: capture pads to `max_batch_size + 1`, but replays are unpadded, so the buckets differ once `max_batch_size >= 8`.\n  - FlashInfer now uses `_pad_flashinfer_cu_seqlens_buffer`.\n  - Other backends keep the existing `pad_cu_seqlens`.\n\n## Validation\n\n```shell\npytest tests/v1/cudagraph/test_encoder_cudagraph.py -v\n\n# 99 passed in 30.30s\n```\n\n## Details\n\nThere is no model architectures left:\n\n- DeepSeek-V4.1 and MiniMax-M3 reject FlashInfer when encoder CG is on.\n- Qwen3-Omni is covered by #63809.\n- Kimi-K3, unlike its predecessor, pads capture and replay to the same size.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
